  "question": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> gas is bubbled through water during a soft drink manufacturing process at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>298</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> exerts a partial pressure of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>835</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>bar</mi></math> then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></math>&nbsp;of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> would dissolve in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math> of water. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math> is _______. (Nearest integer)</p><p>(Henry&#39;s law constant for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>298</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>67</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>bar</mi></math>)</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "25",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>From Henry&#39;s law</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mi>gas</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>&#183;</mo></mrow></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mi>gas</mi></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>835</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>67</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mfenced><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfenced></mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1000</mn></mrow><mn>18</mn></mfrac></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mfenced><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>025</mn></math></p><p>Millimoles of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>025</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1000</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn></math></p>",
